# Python Conventions

- Python 3.12+
- Type hints on public functions and methods
- Pydantic for boundaries (API, tools, agent I/O); dataclasses where appropriate
- Prefer `pathlib.Path` over string paths
- Explicit exceptions; no bare `except:`
- Structured logging (no `print` for operational logs)

## Naming

| Kind | Style |
|------|--------|
| Classes | PascalCase |
| Functions / variables | snake_case |
| Constants | UPPER_SNAKE_CASE |
| Files / modules | snake_case |
| Private members | `_leading_underscore` |

## Avoid

- Wildcard imports (`from x import *`)
- Unexplained magic numbers
- Giant functions or classes
- Mutable global state
- Business logic in Streamlit pages or FastAPI route handlers

## Prefer

- Small, testable units
- Explicit return types
- Skills for deterministic calculations
- Repository layer for persistence
